The RAND study adds to the growing body of scientific literature on the scale of climate change and its impact on the world. The report's authors, scientists and analysts, argue that humanity is now experiencing the early stages of a "gradient catastrophe" — an abrupt worsening of climate change based on the human-caused increase in greenhouse gases in the atmosphere.

